# Build output paths and the size each may reach before the `builds` tool
# deletes it whole for the next build to refill (cargo mostly from sccache).
# scripts/build-layout.sh, run first by the hooks and every build script, links
# each path to /Volumes/Builds/bae/<checkout>/<path> and applies the caps.
#
# Caps are about twice a fresh build of each: host 9.8G, macOS bridge 7.4G,
# Android 6.4G, iOS 12G; the macOS app's .build holds two DerivedData trees
# (check.sh's and run.sh's) of 5.2G each fresh; BaeKit's `swift build` 4.4G;
# the others are under 1G.
#
# path                                cap
target                                20G
target-macos                          15G
target-ios                            24G
target-android                        13G
bae-macos/bae/.build                  20G
bae-ios/bae/.build                    10G
BaeKit/.build                         9G
bae-android/.gradle                   1G
bae-android/app/build                 2G
bae-avalonia/obj                      1G
bae-avalonia/bin                      1G
bae-avalonia/bae-avalonia.Tests/obj   1G
bae-avalonia/bae-avalonia.Tests/bin   1G
